      "description": "The seventh-century-BC Assyrian king Esarhaddon (r. 680\u2013669 BC) had his workmen dismantle the Central Palace of the eighth-century-BC ruler Tiglath-pileser III. Numerous (inscribed and sculpted) limestone wall slabs from that royal residence at Kalhu were reused in the Southwest Palace.",
